 * DISPATCH RULE (see the multi-registrar plan's Phase 2): a domain that
 * already has a DB row must resolve `registrarById(domain.registrar)` and
 * call through THAT registrar only — a domain fulfilled through one backend
 * has no record at the other, so it must never silently fail over. A new
 * search/quote with no DB row yet fans out across `configuredRegistrars()`
 * instead (see `lib/tools/domain-availability.ts`). This module only builds
 * the registry `configuredRegistrars`/`registrarById` read from — it does not
 * itself decide which one a given call site should use.
